#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0253.1 expect=violation domain=RELREC
#note "No DOMAIN column: a real RELREC carries RDOMAIN, and a DOMAIN cell would otherwise be presented as the scope name. Row 1 has RELTYPE populated AND USUBJID populated -> FIRES; row 2 has RELTYPE populated AND IDVARVAL populated -> FIRES; row 3 is a clean domain-to-domain link; row 4 has an empty RELTYPE so the leading conjunct is false (a record-to-record link, CDISC-SEND-0286's business)."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#expectViolationCount 2
#expectViolationAt row=1 RELTYPE=ONE
#expectViolationAt row=2 RELTYPE=MANY
dataset RELREC label="Related Records"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col RDOMAIN  type=Char label="Related Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col POOLID   type=Char label="Pool Identifier"
col IDVAR    type=Char label="Identifying Variable"
col IDVARVAL type=Char label="Identifying Variable Value"
col RELTYPE  type=Char label="Relationship Type"
col RELID    type=Char label="Relationship Identifier"
---
S1 | MA | S1-001 |  | MASEQ |   | ONE  | R1
S1 | MI |        |  | MISEQ | 1 | MANY | R2
S1 | MA |        |  | MASEQ |   | ONE  | R3
S1 | MI | S1-002 |  | MISEQ | 2 |      | R4
---
